From af1367ecf0c593ab68d4a88a339854eb064ca313 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John O'Dell <johncodell14@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:36:10 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] civ45: the tech tree, 92 advances in seven eras with costs
 per era and re-homed unlocks

Freeciv45 tech slice. techs.ruleset: seven tech classes (Ancient,
Classical, Medieval, Renaissance, Industrial, Modern, Information) with
cost_pct 100, 100, 110, 120, 130, 140, 150; every advance names its
class; six advances added (Agriculture, Hunting, Archery, Machinery,
Compass, Printing) with fallback icons; three removed (Ruler Apotheosis,
Nanomaterials, Labor Union); the prerequisites of Physics, Magnetism,
Navigation, Atomic Theory, Genetic Engineering and Fusion Power changed.
buildings.ruleset: Altar to The Divine Ruler needs Monarchy, the Space
Elevator and its Tether Superconductors, Shakespeare's Theatre Printing,
Barracks Warrior Code. units.ruleset: Mech. Inf. needs Robotics.
terrain.ruleset: irrigation needs Agriculture. README.civ45 says so.
---
 data/civ45/README.civ45      |  10 ++
 data/civ45/buildings.ruleset |   9 +-
 data/civ45/techs.ruleset     | 220 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 data/civ45/terrain.ruleset   |   4 +
 data/civ45/units.ruleset     |   2 +-
 5 files changed, 207 insertions(+), 38 deletions(-)

diff --git a/data/civ45/README.civ45 b/data/civ45/README.civ45
index 97d9d37..d50a3a5 100644
--- a/data/civ45/README.civ45
+++ b/data/civ45/README.civ45
@@ -53,6 +53,16 @@ Differences from sandbox
   2050) and at the start of that turn the living player with the highest
   score is named the winner, so the game ends with a victor rather than a
   turn-limit notice. The thresholds are first values, untuned.
+- The tech tree has 92 advances in seven eras (Ancient, Classical,
+  Medieval, Renaissance, Industrial, Modern, Information), each a tech
+  class whose cost_pct (100, 100, 110, 120, 130, 140, 150) scales the
+  era's costs on top of the Linear style. Six techs are new
+  (Agriculture, Hunting, Archery, Machinery, Compass, Printing), three
+  sandbox leftovers are gone (Ruler Apotheosis, Nanomaterials, Labor
+  Union) and their unlocks moved (Altar to The Divine Ruler to Monarchy,
+  the Space Elevator and its Tether to Superconductors, Mech. Inf. to
+  Robotics); Shakespeare's Theatre needs Printing, Barracks need Warrior
+  Code, and irrigation needs Agriculture.
 - Upgrades keep a unit's veteran levels (sandbox takes one away).
 - Drafting: Levy (Bronze Working, 2/2, 10 shields), Militia (Gunpowder,
   8/8, 20 shields) and Conscripts (Conscription, 14/14, 25 shields) are
